= Authentication — Technical =

Authentication protocols verify possession or use of one or more authenticators under an assurance model. Threat resistance depends on authenticator type, channel security, verifier design, replay resistance, phishing resistance, lifecycle management, and recovery procedures.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* authentication ≠ authorization
* authentication ≠ identity proofing
* authentication ≠ proof of real-world identity in every system

